        <referenceFunction amount="1" category="electronics" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="Data are based on information in an LCA study about OLED matrices for device screens; UUID: 5e8cee0e-ec8e-353d-9454-dac242cf0704" includedProcesses="The source of life cycle inventory for organic light emitting diode (OLED) is the LCA study of Amasawa et al., 2016. Overall, the approaches for constructing inventories of fine specialty chemicals and fabrication process in the OLED for smartphones or other smart devices involve creation of inventory with stoichiometry and application of observed correlation between display area and production cost in the display industry. From this study, four specialty chemicals/ingredients are chosen for organic and metal layer depositions, namely bisphenol-A, phtalic anhydride, magnesium, and silver. The geographical specificity is set to be in South Korea, because the majority of active matrix OLED display productions (&gt;90% of production share) occur in the country according to Semenza, 2013. For such reason, all electricity input reflects the electricity mix of South Korean grid." infrastructureIncluded="false" infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="electronics" localName="OLED module, at plant" localSubCategory="devices" name="OLED module, at plant" subCategory="devices" unit="kg">
